Public filings and derived data
-------------------------------
This repository contains excerpts and data derived from offer documents that issuers and their lead
managers have made public: draft red herring prospectuses, red herring prospectuses, prospectuses
and abridged prospectuses. The documents themselves are not stored here (they are fetched by the
user and kept out of version control). What is stored, and where it came from:

  data/manifest.jsonl, data/sources.toml   the list of public filings used, with each source URL
  labels/                                  hand-written values and page numbers read from those filings
  benchmark/                               answer keys for the screening app's extraction benchmark
  site/briefs.json                         page-cited briefs shown on the demo site
  docs/history/                            notes on how the software read specific public filings

The filings were published at, among others, www.sebi.gov.in, www.bseindia.com, archives.nseindia.com,
and the websites of lead managers (investmentbank.kotak.com, business.bofa.com). Copyright in each
filing remains with its publisher. The excerpts are short quotations and figures, kept for the purpose
of verifying the software against its sources; if you hold rights in one and want it removed, open an
issue or write to the maintainer at venkateshpanda00@gmail.com.

sample_data/ is synthetic: no real company is represented (see sample_data/DISCLAIMER.md).

SME issuers that are the subject of SEBI orders, and test probes, are excluded from the demo site
(tools/build_demo.py, SKIP_IDS).

No advice
---------
IPO Engine is automated analysis of public documents. It is not investment advice, legal advice, a
credit or regulatory opinion, or a certification of any filing or issuer. A figure it shows is a
pointer to a page; check it against the page. The eligibility screening is decision support against
a versioned, explicitly scoped ruleset that has not had a legal review (docs/screening/REGULATORY_VALIDATION.md).
Nothing in this repository submits anything to SEBI, an exchange or a registrar.

Third-party software is used under its own licences; the dependency lists are in uv.lock and
frontend/package-lock.json, and each release attaches a software bill of materials.
